---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'

const homeDescription =
  'Platform engineering for production: AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, IaC. Tighten operations, cut waste, ship platforms your team owns. One senior lead—not a consulting roster.'

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfessionalService',
  name: 'OpsDevCode',
  description: homeDescription,
  url: 'https://opsdevco.de',
  email: 'eric@opsdevco.de',
  areaServed: 'Worldwide',
  serviceType: ['Platform Engineering', 'Cloud Infrastructure', 'FinOps', 'AWS', 'GCP', 'DevOps', 'Kubernetes', 'IaC', 'CI/CD', 'Custom tooling'],
}

---

<BaseLayout
  title="OpsDevCode | Platform Engineering Advisory"
  description={homeDescription}
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap home">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <h1>Platform engineering<br /><span class="highlight">built for production.</span></h1>
          <p class="sub">
            Hands-on <span class="anchor-soft">AWS, GCP, Kubernetes</span>, and IaC—in your environment.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-fit">
            If <span class="anchor-soft">operating the platform</span> competes with shipping product, this is for you.
          </p>
          <ul class="hero-sub-points scan-list">
            <li>Less waste, clearer operations</li>
            <li>Systems your team can run without a long-term dependency</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="hero-diff">
            <span class="key-em">No slides.</span> No fluff. <span class="key-em">Just working systems.</span>
          </p>
          <p class="hero-anti-consulting">
            This isn’t <span class="anchor-soft">traditional consulting</span> — no large teams, no bloated engagements,
            no unnecessary layers.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-anti-consulting-follow">
            <span class="anchor-soft">Hands-on work in your stack</span>—no bench, no extra layers.
          </p>
          <div class="cta">
            <a class="btn primary" href="https://calendly.com/eric-opsdevco/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a discovery call</a>
            <a class="btn" href="/about#contact">Email me directly</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-reassure">One call to align scope and fit.</p>
          <p class="hero-cred">Solo practice.</p>
          <p class="hero-cred">Senior platform work: AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, IaC, delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section primary-problem home-flow home-flow--clarity" aria-labelledby="primary-problem-heading">
        <h2 id="primary-problem-heading" class="section-title">
          Most teams don’t have a DevOps problem — they have a <span class="anchor-soft">complexity problem</span>.
        </h2>
        <ul class="primary-problem-points scan-list">
          <li>
            Tool sprawl, unclear ownership, <span class="anchor-soft">rising cloud spend</span>, and delivery drag.
          </li>
          <li>
            Platform work should <span class="anchor-soft">cut complexity</span>—not add headcount or tooling theater.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section sounds-familiar home-flow home-flow--clarity" aria-labelledby="sounds-familiar-heading">
        <h2 id="sounds-familiar-heading" class="section-title">If this sounds familiar</h2>
        <ul class="sounds-familiar-list scan-list">
          <li>Infrastructure <span class="anchor-soft">drifted into sprawl</span>—ownership is fuzzy</li>
          <li>CI/CD is <span class="anchor-soft">slow or brittle</span> when you need it predictable</li>
          <li>Cloud spend <span class="anchor-soft">climbs</span> without attributable line items</li>
          <li>Engineering time goes to <span class="anchor-soft">keeping the lights on</span>, not shipping</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section audience home-flow home-flow--clarity" aria-labelledby="who-for-heading">
        <h2 id="who-for-heading" class="section-title">Who this is for</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-2col">
          <div class="tile tile--with-icon">
            <span class="home-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z" />
                <path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5" />
                <path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5" />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <p>
              <strong>AWS, GCP, or Kubernetes</strong> estates where run cost outweighs the leverage you get from the
              platform.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="tile tile--with-icon">
            <span class="home-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2" />
                <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4" />
                <path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75" />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <p>
              <strong>Engineering leaders</strong> who need depth without a consulting bench or account team.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="tile tile--with-icon">
            <span class="home-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M22 12h-4l-3 9L9 3l-3 9H2" />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <p>Teams <strong>constrained by delivery</strong>, opaque infrastructure, or runaway cloud spend.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section point-of-view home-flow home-flow--clarity" aria-labelledby="point-of-view-heading">
        <h2 id="point-of-view-heading" class="section-title">Point of view</h2>
        <ul class="point-of-view-points scan-list">
          <li>
            Too much DevOps work optimizes for <span class="kw">tools</span> instead of <span class="kw">outcomes</span>.
          </li>
          <li>
            I <strong class="key-em">cut complexity</strong>, make tradeoffs explicit, and ship systems your team can
            run.
          </li>
          <li>Nothing that only reads well on a <span class="kw">diagram</span>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section before-after home-flow home-flow--clarity" aria-labelledby="before-after-heading">
        <h2 id="before-after-heading" class="section-title">Before / After</h2>
        <div class="split before-after-split">
          <div class="before-after-panel is-before">
            <h3 class="before-after-label">Before</h3>
            <ul class="before-after-list scan-list">
              <li><span class="anchor-soft">Messy</span> infrastructure and unclear ownership</li>
              <li><span class="anchor-soft">Slow</span> or fragile CI/CD pipelines</li>
              <li><span class="anchor-soft">Rising</span> cloud costs with poor visibility</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="before-after-panel is-after">
            <h3 class="before-after-label">After</h3>
            <ul class="before-after-list scan-list">
              <li><span class="anchor-soft">Clear</span> systems your team can own and change</li>
              <li><span class="anchor-soft">Faster</span>, more reliable delivery</li>
              <li><span class="anchor-soft">Better</span> cost visibility and less operational friction</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section trust home-flow home-flow--trust" aria-labelledby="trust-heading">
        <h2 id="trust-heading" class="section-title">Hands-on practice</h2>
        <p class="trust-operator">
          <span class="home-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="4" rx="1" />
              <rect x="2" y="10" width="20" height="4" rx="1" />
              <rect x="2" y="17" width="20" height="4" rx="1" />
              <path d="M6 5v.01M6 12v.01M6 19v.01" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span>
            Built by someone who has <span class="anchor-soft">run this in production</span>—not briefed it in slides.
          </span>
        </p>
        <div class="testimonial">
          <ul class="trust-points scan-list">
            <li>Operator-first: ship changes, not slide reviews.</li>
            <li>AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, IaC, delivery, light tooling—hands-on.</li>
            <li>Clear ownership; outcomes that survive after the engagement.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="fine trust-about-link"><a href="/about">About</a> — background and how to reach me.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section how-work home-flow home-flow--clarity" aria-labelledby="how-work-heading">
        <h2 id="how-work-heading" class="section-title">How I work</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-2col">
          <div class="tile">
            <p><strong>Fixed scope, clear outcomes</strong>—time-boxed engagements.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tile">
            <p><strong>Engineering, not decks.</strong></p>
            <ul class="tile-inline-points scan-list">
              <li>Depth on AWS, GCP, Kubernetes, and IaC</li>
              <li>Direct work, no firm overhead</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="tile">
            <p><strong>Advise, pair, or ship code</strong>—scope follows the problem.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tile">
            <p><strong>Systems your team still runs</strong> when the engagement ends.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section services-section home-flow home-flow--outcomes">
        <h2 class="section-title">Services</h2>
        <ul class="services-lede scan-list">
          <li>Not advisory-only.</li>
          <li>Work happens <span class="kw">in your repos and clusters</span>, beside your engineers.</li>
          <li>Outcomes you can <strong class="key-em">measure and own</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="grid grid-2col">
          <a href="/services/platform-health" class="tile">
            <h3>Platform Health Check</h3>
            <p>Find bottlenecks, risk, and avoidable complexity—then prioritize what to fix first.</p>
            <p class="tile-desc-follow">A concrete remediation path, not a generic report.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/finops" class="tile">
            <h3>FinOps</h3>
            <p>Cut waste and get spend attributable to teams, services, and resources.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/iac" class="tile">
            <h3>IaC</h3>
            <p>Standardize IaC so changes are reviewable, repeatable, and safer to ship.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/cicd" class="tile">
            <h3>CI/CD</h3>
            <p>Faster, more reliable delivery through pipelines your team can maintain.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/custom-tooling" class="tile">
            <h3>Custom tooling</h3>
            <p>Small internal tools that remove toil—automation where it earns its keep.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/agentic" class="tile">
            <h3>Agentic Development</h3>
            <p>Agent-assisted workflows where they reduce error and cycle time.</p>
            <p class="tile-desc-follow">Measured adoption—not novelty for its own sake.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="services-cta-link">
          <a class="btn" href="/services">All services</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section example-outcomes home-flow home-flow--outcomes" aria-labelledby="example-outcomes-heading">
        <h2 id="example-outcomes-heading" class="section-title">Outcomes in practice</h2>
        <ul class="example-outcomes-list scan-list">
          <li>
            <span class="anchor-soft">Cut</span> cloud spend by removing waste and misconfiguration—not blanket downsizing
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="anchor-soft">Hardened</span> delivery pipelines; fewer failed deploys and rollbacks
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="anchor-soft">Aligned</span> IaC with how teams own and change infrastructure
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="anchor-soft">Shipped</span> small tools that removed recurring operational toil
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section tools-section home-flow home-flow--outcomes">
        <h2 class="section-title">Tools</h2>
        <p class="note tools-intro">
          <span class="home-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path
                d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span>
            Open-source utilities for sharp edges in
            <span class="anchor-soft">AWS, Kubernetes, and Terraform</span>—nothing ceremonial.
          </span>
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-2col">
          <a href="https://github.com/opsdevcode/term-dx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="tile">
            <h3>term-dx</h3>
            <p>Diagnose resources stuck in Terminating.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/opsdevcode/knode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="tile">
            <h3>knode</h3>
            <p>List and cordon/drain EKS nodes from CLI.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="tools-cta-link">
          <a class="btn" href="/tools">All tools</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section engagement-flow home-flow home-flow--action" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading">
        <h2 id="how-it-works-heading" class="section-title">How it works</h2>
        <ol class="engagement-steps">
          <li class="engagement-step">
            <span class="engagement-step-index" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <div class="engagement-step-body">
              <p class="engagement-step-text">
                <strong>Discovery call</strong>
                <span class="engagement-step-line">Current state, constraints, and priority order.</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="engagement-step">
            <span class="engagement-step-index" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <div class="engagement-step-body">
              <p class="engagement-step-text">
                <strong>Focused engagement</strong>
                <span class="engagement-step-line"
                  >Time-boxed work on the highest-leverage gap—not a roadmap science project.</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="engagement-step">
            <span class="engagement-step-index" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <div class="engagement-step-body">
              <p class="engagement-step-text">
                <strong>Practical outcomes</strong>
                <span class="engagement-step-line">Changes your team can run—without a standing retainer.</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <ul class="engagement-follow scan-list" aria-label="How engagements are structured">
          <li>Fixed scope; outcomes defined up front.</li>
          <li>From a short assessment to focused implementation—your call.</li>
          <li>Meaningful movement in weeks, not quarters.</li>
          <li>No dependency model: systems your team can operate and explain.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section closing-cta home-flow home-flow--finale" aria-labelledby="closing-cta-heading">
        <p class="closing-cta-kicker">When you&apos;re ready</p>
        <h2 id="closing-cta-heading" class="closing-cta-title">Book a 30-minute discovery call</h2>
        <div class="cta">
          <a
            class="btn primary"
            href="https://calendly.com/eric-opsdevco/30min"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a discovery call</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/about#contact">Email me directly</a>
        </div>
        <p class="closing-cta-support">
          Low stakes: confirm fit, scope, and whether working together is worth a follow-up.
        </p>
      </section>

      <Footer />
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
